"""Approximate an s-related interaction across token boundaries.

After an s-like ending, repeated s initials are negative, while h/l/u/w/y/z
initials are generally positive. Longer pieces attenuate the response;
interior s letters subtract from it. Letter and syllable groups extend this
spelling rule approximately across scripts, without a word/token table.
Possessive s, isolated space-prefixed s, and document-initial s have separate
negative responses. Carry resets at document boundaries; lone NUL bytes
return zero and preserve the preceding token.
