"""Predict a negative response to short Latin fragments built around L.

L followed by another consonant is strongest, especially LR. Single L,
vowel syllables and doubled L are weak. The lex-/glycer- root spellings,
Slavic -lov/-loff endings, and LDL are strong special cases. Longer L
fragments get smaller responses. Reasoning and tool tags are separate.
At a document start the prediction is a small constant instead.
This is a spelling approximation; most other tokens stay near zero.
