"""Respond to decimal digits, dot leaders, and conversation boundaries.

The largest ordinary-text response is to a single ASCII digit immediately
following a period, especially a zero. It is stronger when the period follows
another digit, weaker for a bare period, and suppressed in .sub./.sup. markup.
Spaced runs of periods also respond. Chat-start and reasoning markers have
separate levels. Short word-internal n-final endings get a small positive
response, especially a final n split off after w. Other lexical responses
are approximated by zero.
